W:
W: "Mer redet n\"ot T\"utsch und Franz\"osisch durenand, das w\"ar denn schon n\"od gommilfo".
W:(You don't speak German and French at the same time, that wouldn't be <comme il faut>)
W: that funny thing here is that the expression uses German and French in the same sentence
W: cf. comme il faut (fr. 'properly, duly')
